\ p2p.fam — tabminer's peer protocol over UDP (docs/NODE.md, step 6), after
\ the node's other words.  As tabminer's miner/src/net.rs: every datagram
\ is "TAB1", a type byte and a little-endian payload, at most 1,232 bytes.
\ A request carries the token the peer gave us in its last Ping or Pong; a
\ peer serves requests only from an address that answered its Ping with
\ the nonce echoed, so every Ping is answered, whoever sends it.  Our
\ token for an address is a keyed hash of it (ptokn), as tabminer's
\ token_for, so a request with it shows it came from there.  Anyone with
\ their token is answered GetPeers (the peers that answered us) and, as
\ docs/TABERNACLE.md has it, GetImages and GetImage: the image this
\ machine booted (/dev/image), as the version in its /lib/version, in
\ 1,024-byte chunks, 64 an ask at most.  Up to PPEERS peers, one
\ the current (puse): requests go to it and only its replies are taken;
\ meanwhile any peer's Pings are answered, its requests for pooled
\ transactions served (GetChunks, kind 1, with our token), and its
\ announcements of transactions (TxInv) queued for the relay (pinq).
\
\ Blocks, manifests and parts come as 1,024-byte chunks, asked for in
\ windows of PWIN: the guest's socket queues eight datagrams, and more in
\ flight would be dropped.  The next window is asked for as soon as the
\ last has come; only a chunk lost waits (300 ms), then is asked again.  Headers come as up to ten datagrams of six,
\ from a height; those lost are asked for again from the first gap.
\
\ pinit ( ip port lport -- )  the socket (bound to lport) and peer 0,
\ the current; the image to serve, if any; padd ( ip port -- k ) another; puse ( k -- ) the current.
\ pping ( -- flag )  a Ping to the current peer until its Pong (a few
\ seconds): its status in pst.
\ pann ( id k -- )  TxInv (id: 32 canonical bytes) to every peer that
\ answered but k.
\ pkeep  each peer pinged when its time comes, as tabminer does: every
\ 30 s while it answers; one that has not answered within 35 s again
\ after 2 s, then 4, 8 and so on to 30, for good (a peer restarted forgets
\ us until we ping it).  Silent for 180 s it is said lost (with vrb), and
\ back when it answers.
\ pdeq ( -- e | 0 )  the oldest queued announcement: its id (32 bytes),
\ then its peer; valid until the next pwait.
\ phdrs ( h -- n )  up to 60 main-chain headers from height h, into phb in
\ order: how many arrived without a gap.
\ pfetch ( kind part id -- a n | 0 0 )  an object: a block (kind 0), the
\ manifest (2) or part `part` (3) of the snapshot after block id
\ (canonical words); malloc'd.
\ pwait ( ns -- type | 0 )  the next datagram from the peer, in prx (Pings
\ answered, Pongs taken, meanwhile).
\ Our status (myh, mytip, mywork, mygen) is the caller's to keep.

: pfd variable ;  : pip variable ;  : ppt variable ;
: ptok variable ;  : mtok variable ;  : mnon variable ;  : pst variable ;  : pok variable ;
: ptx variable ;  : ptp variable ;  : prx variable ;  : prn variable ;  : pent variable ;  : pfrom variable ;
: phb variable ;  : phh variable ;  : pgot variable ;  : prnd variable ;
: pobj variable ;  : plen variable ;  : pcnt variable ;  : pmap variable ;  : pkind variable ;  : ppart variable ;  : pid variable ;
: pidle variable ;  : pnew variable ;  : pxfd variable ;  : pxrdy variable ;
: ptab variable ;  : pnp variable ;  : pcur variable ;  : pfk variable ;
: pinq variable ;  : pinh variable ;  : pint variable ;  : pidm variable ;  : pgb variable ;  : pgn variable ;
: myh variable ;  : mytip variable ;  : mywork variable ;  : mygen variable ;
: pkey variable ;  : pkd variable ;  : pko variable ;  : pifd variable ;  : pisz variable ;  : pver variable ;  : pisent variable ;

:M PWIN 4 lit ;                               \ chunks in flight
:M PMAX 400000 lit ;                          \ the largest object taken: 4 MiB
:M PPEERS 4 lit ;

\ Writing a datagram at ptx.
: w8  ptp @ c!  ptp @ 1 lit + ptp ! ;
: w16  dup w8 8 lit rshift w8 ;
: w32  dup w16 10 lit rshift w16 ;
: w64  swap w32 w32 ;                         \ ( lo hi -- )
: wbs  tuck ptp @ swap bcopy  ptp @ + ptp ! ;  \ ( a n -- )
: wbeg  ptx @ ptp !  54 lit w8 41 lit w8 42 lit w8 31 lit w8  w8 ;   \ ( type -- )
: wsendto  begin pfd @ ptx @ ptp @ ptx @ - 4 lit pick 4 lit pick sendto FFFFFF8F lit = while 5F5E100 lit sleep repeat 2drop ;   \ ( ip port -- )
: wsend  pip @ ppt @ wsendto ;
: wtok  ptok @ 8 lit wbs ;                     \ the peer's token for us

\ ptokn ( ip port -- )  mtok = our token for that address: the first 8
\ bytes of compress(key, address), the key random at start.
: ptokn
pkd @ 8 lit wzero  pkd @ 2 lit w!  dup FFFF lit and pkd @ 0 lit w!  10 lit rshift pkd @ 1 lit w!
pkey @ pkd @ pko @ compress  pko @ mtok @ 8 lit bcopy ;

\ wstatus ( nonce -- )  our status, with the nonce at its address and
\ mtok's token (ptokn for whom it goes to).
: wstatus
8 lit wbs  A lit w32  mtok @ 8 lit wbs  mygen @ 20 lit wbs
myh @ w32  myh @ 1 lit + w32  mytip @ 20 lit wbs  mywork @ 20 lit wbs
A lit 0 lit w64  A lit 0 lit w64 ;

: prec  C0 lit * ptab @ + ;                     \ ( k -- a )  ip, port, answered, 0, token (8), status (8C),
\ then (pkeep's, in secs) when to ping it next (A4), the wait after that
\ (A8), when it last answered (AC), whether said lost (B0)
: psend  prec dup @ swap 4 lit + @ wsendto ;    \ ( k -- )  the datagram at ptx to peer k
: puse  dup pcur !  prec  dup @ pip !  dup 4 lit + @ ppt !  dup 10 lit + ptok !  18 lit + pst ! ;
: padd  pnp @ prec  tuck 4 lit + !  !  0 lit pnp @ prec 8 lit + !  pnp @ prec A4 lit + 4 lit wzero  pnp @ dup 1 lit + pnp ! ;   \ ( ip port -- k )
\ pwho ( ip port -- k | -1 )
: pwho
FFFFFFFF lit pfk !
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do  over i prec @ =  over i prec 4 lit + @ = and if i pfk ! then  loop then
2drop pfk @ ;

: pinit  ( ip port lport -- )
1 lit socket pfd !  pfd @ swap 1 lit swap 0 lit swap net drop   \ bound to lport
600 lit alloc ptx !  800 lit alloc prx !  10 lit alloc pent !  0 lit pxfd !  0 lit pxrdy !  10 lit alloc pfrom !
10 lit alloc mtok !  10 lit alloc mnon !
BF40 lit alloc phb !  40 lit alloc pgot !
PPEERS C0 lit * alloc ptab !  0 lit pnp !  240 lit alloc pinq !  0 lit pinh !  0 lit pint !  20 lit alloc pidm !
padd puse
\ our tokens' key and our nonce: random
p2init  20 lit alloc pkey !  20 lit alloc pkd !  20 lit alloc pko !
"/dev/random" 0 lit open dup pkey @ 20 lit read drop dup mnon @ 8 lit read drop close drop
8 lit 0 lit do pkey @ i 2 lit lshift + dup @ 7FFFFFF lit and swap ! loop
\ the image: its size, and the version it says it is
0 lit pisz !
"/dev/image" 0 lit open dup 0< if drop else
	dup pifd !
	"/lib/version" 0 lit open dup 0< if drop else
		dup pko @ 1F lit read dup 0< if drop 0 lit then pko @ + 0 lit swap c!  close drop
		pko @ c@ 30 lit - A lit u< if pko @ atoi pver !  pifd @ 0 lit 2 lit seek pisz ! then
	then
then ;

\ d8= ( a b n -- flag )  n bytes equal.
: d8=  -1 lit swap 0 lit do 2 lit pick i + c@ 2 lit pick i + c@ = and loop nip nip ;

\ prdy ( ns -- flag )  a datagram waiting within ns; or, sooner, the
\ descriptor in pxfd (if any: the API's listener) readable, pxrdy set.
: prdy
pfd @ pent @ !  1 lit pent @ 4 lit + !  pxfd @ pent @ 8 lit + !  1 lit pent @ C lit + !
pent @ pxfd @ if 2 lit else 1 lit then rot poll 0 lit > if
	pent @ C lit + @ 10 lit rshift 0= 0= pxfd @ 0= 0= and pxrdy !
	pent @ 4 lit + @ 10 lit rshift 0= 0=
else 0 lit then ;

: u16@  dup c@ swap 1 lit + c@ 8 lit lshift or ;   \ ( a -- x )
\ pcko ( index -- )  chunk index of the transaction at pgb (pgn bytes),
\ if there is one, to peer pfk.
: pcko
dup A lit lshift dup pgn @ u< if
	9 lit wbeg  1 lit w8  prx @ E lit + 20 lit wbs  pgn @ w32  swap w16
	pgn @ over - dup 400 lit u> if drop 400 lit then  dup w16  swap pgb @ + swap wbs
	pfk @ psend
else 2drop then ;
\ pgive  the GetChunks in prx: the chunks of a pooled transaction, if it
\ carries our token.
: pgive
prx @ 5 lit + mtok @ 8 lit d8=  prx @ D lit + c@ 1 lit = and  prn @ 2F lit u< 0= and if
	prx @ E lit + pidm @ dle  pidm @ qfind dup 0< if drop else
		qslot dup @ pgb !  4 lit + @ pgn !
		prx @ 2E lit + c@  dup 2 lit lshift 2F lit + prn @ u> if drop 0 lit then
		?dup if 0 lit do
			prx @ 2F lit + i 2 lit lshift +  dup u16@ swap 2 lit + u16@
			dup if over + swap do i pcko loop else 2drop then
		loop then
	then
then ;
\ pqinv  the TxInv in prx queued (16 at most).
: pqinv
pint @ 10 lit u< prn @ 25 lit u< 0= and if
	pinh @ pint @ + F lit and 24 lit * pinq @ +
	prx @ 5 lit + over 20 lit bcopy  pfk @ swap 20 lit + !
	pint @ 1 lit + pint !
then ;
: pdeq  pint @ if pinh @ 24 lit * pinq @ +  pinh @ 1 lit + F lit and pinh !  pint @ 1 lit - pint ! else 0 lit then ;

\ prply  the datagram at ptx to whoever sent the one in prx.
: prply  pfrom @ @ pfrom @ 4 lit + @ wsendto ;
\ ppeers  Peers: those that answered us, as they are reached from here.
: ppeers
4 lit wbeg  ptp @ 0 lit w8  0 lit
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i prec 8 lit + @ if
		i prec @  dup 18 lit rshift w8  dup 10 lit rshift w8  dup 8 lit rshift w8  w8  i prec 4 lit + @ w16  1 lit +
	then
loop then
swap c!  prply ;
\ pimgs  Images: our version and its size, or none.
: pimgs  41 lit wbeg  pisz @ if 1 lit w8 pver @ w32 pisz @ w32 else 0 lit w8 then prply ;
\ pichunk ( index -- )  ImageChunk index, if the image has it and fewer
\ than 64 went for this ask.
: pichunk
dup A lit lshift dup pisz @ u<  pisent @ 40 lit u< and if
	43 lit wbeg  pver @ w32  pisz @ w32  over w16
	pisz @ over - dup 400 lit u> if drop 400 lit then  dup w16
	swap pifd @ swap 0 lit seek drop
	pifd @ ptp @ rot read  dup 0< if drop 0 lit then  ptp @ + ptp !
	drop prply  pisent @ 1 lit + pisent !
else 2drop then ;
\ pimage  the GetImage in prx: token, version, count, then start and
\ length (u16 each) for each range.
: pimage
prx @ D lit + le@ pver @ =  pisz @ 0= 0= and
prx @ 11 lit + c@  dup 2 lit lshift 12 lit + prn @ =  rot and if
	0 lit pisent !
	?dup if 0 lit do
		prx @ 12 lit + i 2 lit lshift +  dup u16@ swap 2 lit + u16@
		dup if over + swap do i pichunk loop else 2drop then
	loop then
else drop then ;

\ pshow ( k -- )  peer k's address.
: pshow
prec dup @  dup 18 lit rshift u. 2E lit putc  dup 10 lit rshift FF lit and u. 2E lit putc
dup 8 lit rshift FF lit and u. 2E lit putc  FF lit and u. 3A lit putc  4 lit + @ u. ;

\ pwait ( ns -- type | 0 )
: pwait
prdy if
	pfd @ prx @ 800 lit pfrom @ recvfrom prn !
	pfrom @ @ pfrom @ 4 lit + @ 2dup pwho drop ptokn
	prn @ 5 lit u< prx @ @ 31424154 lit <> or if 0 lit else
		prx @ 4 lit + c@
		dup 1 lit =  prn @ 91 lit u< 0= and if  2 lit wbeg  prx @ 5 lit + wstatus  prply  then
		prn @ D lit u< 0=  prx @ 5 lit + mtok @ 8 lit d8= and if
			dup 3 lit = prn @ D lit = and if ppeers then
			dup 40 lit = prn @ D lit = and if pimgs then
			dup 42 lit = if pimage then
		then
		pfk @ 0< if drop 0 lit else
		dup 2 lit = if
			prx @ 5 lit + mnon @ 8 lit d8= if
				prx @ 5 lit + pfk @ prec 18 lit + 8C lit bcopy  prx @ 11 lit + pfk @ prec 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy
				1 lit pfk @ prec 8 lit + !  pfk @ pcur @ = if 1 lit pok ! then
				secs pfk @ prec AC lit + !
				pfk @ prec B0 lit + @ if 0 lit pfk @ prec B0 lit + !  vrb @ if nhead "peer " puts pfk @ pshow " back" puts 0A lit putc then then
			then
		then
		dup 8 lit = if pgive then
		dup A lit = if pqinv then
		pfk @ pcur @ = 0= if drop 0 lit then
		then
	then
else 0 lit then ;

\ pkeep
: pkt variable ;
: pkeep
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	secs pkt !
	pkt @ i prec A4 lit + @ - 0< 0= if
		i prec @ i prec 4 lit + @ ptokn  1 lit wbeg  mnon @ wstatus  i psend
		pkt @ i prec AC lit + @ - 23 lit u< i prec AC lit + @ and if 1E lit else
			i prec A8 lit + @ 1 lit lshift  dup 2 lit u< if drop 2 lit then  dup 1E lit u> if drop 1E lit then
		then
		dup i prec A8 lit + !  pkt @ + i prec A4 lit + !
		pkt @ i prec AC lit + @ - B4 lit u> i prec B0 lit + @ 0= and if
			1 lit i prec B0 lit + !  vrb @ if nhead "peer " puts i pshow " lost: silent 180 s, still asking" puts 0A lit putc then
		then
	then
loop then ;

\ pann ( id k -- )
: pann
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	dup i = 0=  i prec 8 lit + @ and if  A lit wbeg  over 20 lit wbs  i psend  then
loop then 2drop ;

: pping
0 lit pok !
8 lit 0 lit do
	pok @ 0= if
		pip @ ppt @ ptokn  1 lit wbeg  mnon @ wstatus  wsend
		A lit 0 lit do pok @ 0= if 5F5E100 lit pwait drop then loop
	then
loop pok @ ;
: pst-h  pst @ 34 lit + @ ;                   \ ( -- h )  the peer's height

\ phdrs ( h -- n )
: pgap  0 lit begin dup 3C lit u< if dup pgot @ + c@ else 0 lit then while 1 lit + repeat ;   \ ( -- g )
: phdrs
phh !  pgot @ 10 lit wzero  0 lit prnd !
begin
	pgap  dup 3C lit u<  over phh @ + pst-h 1 lit + u< and  prnd @ 4 lit u< and
while
	B lit wbeg wtok  phh @ + w32 wsend  prnd @ 1 lit + prnd !
	begin 1DCD6500 lit pwait ?dup while
		6 lit = if
			prx @ 5 lit + c@ ?dup if 0 lit do
				prx @ 6 lit + i CC lit * +  dup 20 lit + le@ phh @ -
				dup 3C lit u< if dup pgot @ + 1 lit swap c!  CC lit * phb @ + CC lit bcopy else 2drop then
			loop then
		then
	repeat
repeat
drop pgap ;

\ ── Chunks ──

: pcp variable ;  : pcl variable ;  : pci variable ;  : pcn variable ;
: prc variable ;  : pnr variable ;  : ptk variable ;  : plast variable ;  : pask variable ;  : prcv variable ;
: wkind  pkind @ w8  pkind @ 3 lit = if ppart @ w32 then ;
\ preq  a GetChunks: chunks 0 to PWIN-1 while the length is not known,
\ else the first PWIN missing, as ranges.
: preq
8 lit wbeg wtok wkind pid @ 20 lit wbs
pobj @ 0= if
	1 lit w8 0 lit w16 PWIN w16  PWIN pask !
else
	ptp @ prc !  0 lit w8
	0 lit pnr !  0 lit ptk !  FFFFFFFE lit plast !
	pcnt @ 0 lit do
		ptk @ PWIN u< i pmap @ + c@ 0= and if
			i plast @ 1 lit + = if ptp @ 2 lit - dup c@ 1 lit + swap c! else i w16 1 lit w16 pnr @ 1 lit + pnr ! then
			i plast !  ptk @ 1 lit + ptk !
		then
	loop
	pnr @ prc @ c!  ptk @ pask !
then
0 lit prcv !
wsend ;

\ pchunk  the Chunk in prx, if it is of the object being fetched.
: pchunk
prx @ 5 lit + pcp !
pcp @ c@ pkind @ =
pkind @ 3 lit = if pcp @ 1 lit + le@ ppart @ = and  pcp @ 5 lit + pcp ! else pcp @ 1 lit + pcp ! then
pcp @ pid @ 20 lit d8= and if
	pcp @ 20 lit + le@ pcl !  pcp @ 24 lit + u16@ pci !  pcp @ 26 lit + u16@ pcn !
	pobj @ 0= pcl @ 1 lit - PMAX u< and if
		pcl @ dup plen !  malloc pobj !  pcl @ 3FF lit + A lit rshift dup pcnt !  dup malloc dup pmap !  swap 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
	then
	pobj @ if
		pcl @ plen @ =  pci @ pcnt @ u< and
		pci @ 1 lit + pcnt @ = if plen @ pci @ A lit lshift - else 400 lit then pcn @ = and
		pcp @ prx @ - 28 lit + pcn @ + prn @ u> 0= and
		dup if drop pci @ pmap @ + c@ 0= then
		if
			pcp @ 28 lit + pobj @ pci @ A lit lshift + pcn @ bcopy  1 lit pci @ pmap @ + c!  1 lit pnew !  prcv @ 1 lit + prcv !
		then
	then
then ;
: pdone  -1 lit pcnt @ 0 lit do i pmap @ + c@ 0= 0= and loop ;

: pfetch  ( kind part id -- a n | 0 0 )
pid ! ppart ! pkind !  0 lit pobj !  0 lit plen !  0 lit pidle !
begin
	pobj @ if pdone 0= else -1 lit then  pidle @ 1E lit u< and
while
	preq  0 lit pnew !
	\ until what was asked for has come (then the next ask at once), or
	\ 300 ms pass with nothing (one lost: asked for again)
	begin
		prcv @ pask @ u<  pobj @ if pdone 0= and then
		if 11E1A300 lit pwait else 0 lit then
	?dup while 9 lit = if pchunk then repeat
	pnew @ if 0 lit pidle ! else pidle @ 1 lit + pidle ! then
repeat
pobj @ if
	pmap @ free
	pdone if pobj @ plen @ else pobj @ free 0 lit 0 lit then
else 0 lit 0 lit then ;
